{
  "_type": "Project",
  "_id": "c4-project-0001",
  "name": "ProductVideo — C4",
  "ownedElements": [
    {
      "_type": "UMLModel",
      "_id": "c4-model-0002",
      "_parent": {
        "$ref": "c4-project-0001"
      },
      "name": "Demo Video Pipeline",
      "documentation": "C4 model of the ProductVideo repo — the scripted pipeline that turns a plain-English flow into a narrated, branded MP4.\n\nLevels: 1 System Context, 2 Containers, 3 Components (every container drawn).\n\nGenerated from docs/c4-model.mjs — edit that and re-run rather than editing the generated files.\n\nThe Express scaffold in sample-app/ (app.js, routes/, views/, bin/) is an untouched express-generator skeleton, not part of this system, and is deliberately not modelled.",
      "ownedElements": [
        {
          "_type": "UMLProfile",
          "_id": "c4-profile-0003",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "C4",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLStereotype",
              "_id": "c4-st-0004",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-profile-0003"
              },
              "name": "person"
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLStereotype",
              "_id": "c4-st-0005",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-profile-0003"
              },
              "name": "software system"
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLStereotype",
              "_id": "c4-st-0006",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-profile-0003"
              },
              "name": "external system"
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLStereotype",
              "_id": "c4-st-0007",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-profile-0003"
              },
              "name": "container"
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLStereotype",
              "_id": "c4-st-0008",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-profile-0003"
              },
              "name": "file store"
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLStereotype",
              "_id": "c4-st-0009",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-profile-0003"
              },
              "name": "component"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-0010",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "1 — System Context",
          "documentation": "Who uses the pipeline and what it depends on. Everything outside the one blue box is somebody else's software.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0011",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0010"
              },
              "name": "Demo author",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0004"
              },
              "documentation": "Developer or PM. Writes the flow in plain English or as a .demo script, points it at a deployment with a target, and builds the video: one stage at a time from a shell, or every part of a video with one build command. Nothing is delivered until it passes the quality gate and the video-qa review."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0012",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0010"
              },
              "name": "Viewer",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0004"
              },
              "documentation": "Prospect, customer or internal audience. Watches the finished MP4; never touches the pipeline."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0013",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0010"
              },
              "name": "Demo Video Pipeline",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0005"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: Node.js CLI stages\n\nTurns a plain-English flow into a narrated, branded MP4. Drives a real browser, captures frames and input telemetry, then assembles, zooms, composites, narrates, tightens and cards the result. The stages run one at a time by hand, or all of them per video through the build orchestrator; every video is measured by the quality gate before it is called done."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0014",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0010"
              },
              "name": "Web application under demo",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0006"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: Any web app\n\nThe deployment being recorded — localhost, staging, a customer sandbox, or a third-party app such as claude.ai. Named by a target; may require signing in. Flows run against live data, so the pipeline hovers rather than clicking anything destructive."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0015",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0010"
              },
              "name": "Google Chrome",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0006"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: Chrome + DevTools Protocol\n\nDriven by puppeteer-core on a dedicated user-data profile — one per target, so a login survives between takes and a video can show two signed-in users without anyone signing in on camera. Frames come from Page.startScreencast. The cursor in the finished video is synthesized from telemetry rather than recorded, so the capture needs no real cursor."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0016",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0010"
              },
              "name": "ffmpeg / ffprobe",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0006"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: Local CLI\n\nOn PATH, or via FFMPEG / FFPROBE. Every encode, decode, probe and audio filter graph. The compositor also pipes raw RGBA through it in both directions, so no intermediate frame hits disk."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0017",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0010"
              },
              "name": "Claude in Chrome extension",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0006"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: Browser extension\n\nDrives the user own Chrome, with their own session, so there is no SSO ritual and no email code to fill. Used before a take to turn the natural-language ask selectors in a script into concrete ones against the live DOM. It cannot record: it has screenshot capture but no screencast, so the take itself stays with the CDP driver."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0018",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0010"
              },
              "name": "Text-to-speech API",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0006"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ElevenLabs or OpenAI\n\nChosen by DEMO_TTS, or by whichever key is set. Anthropic has no TTS API, so this is a third party. Keys come from the shell or .env, never a committed file. The only network dependency other than the app under demo."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0019",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0010"
              },
              "name": "video-qa agent",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0006"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: Claude Code subagent\n\nReviews a finished video: runs the quality gate, then checks every narration line against a still of the screen — is the thing being described on screen while it is said? — and returns PASS or FAIL with the fix for each defect. Read-only. Defined in .claude/agents/video-qa.md."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClassDiagram",
              "_id": "c4-dgm-0020",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0010"
              },
              "name": "C4-L1 — System Context",
